cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use aastex in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: aastex
abstract: >-
  aastex is a Python library for writing articles for the journals of the
  American Astronomical Society as Python programs. It extends PyLaTeX with
  the parts of the AASTeX class that a manuscript needs. Figures are drawn by
  the code that produced the result, and quantities in the text are LaTeX
  macros computed from Python values, so an article cannot drift from the
  analysis behind it.
authors:
  - family-names: Smart
    given-names: Roy T.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9997-5515"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sun-data/aastex"
url: "https://aastex.readthedocs.io"
license: BSD-3-Clause
keywords:
  - AASTeX
  - LaTeX
  - scientific writing
